course: dictionary
lesson: 11599
title: A name with a formal title
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An appellation is a formal word for a name or title. You will meet it in old books, in news stories and on bottles and packets. «The ship had the appellation "Silver Star".» Here the word means the name given to the ship. Swap in name and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Everyday words to use instead are «name» and «title». «Her full appellation was Dame Anne Clarke.» A formal name can sound grand, like a title given to an important person, but it still means a name.
explain: Some appellations are protected by law. Champagne is the protected name for sparkling wine made in one region of France, so the word tells you where the wine truly comes from. «The label showed the appellation Champagne» means the official name of the place the wine came from.
fact: Appellation means a name or title given to someone or something.
fact: «Appellation» is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in books, speeches and labels.
fact: Everyday synonyms for appellation are «name» and «title».
fact: An appellation can also be a protected name for where a wine or food comes from, such as Champagne.
fact: A good check is to swap in «name» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The ship's appellation was Silver Star.» What does appellation mean here? | A map | A sail | A sea storm | *A name
exercise: Which everyday word is a simple swap for appellation? | Bottle | Cloud | Engine | *Title
exercise: «The label showed the appellation Champagne, so the wine came from that region.» What does the appellation tell us? | The number of guests | *The protected name showing where the wine comes from | The colour of the bottle | The price of the bottle
test: «Her full appellation was Dame Anne Clarke.» What is an appellation? | A type of weather | *A name or title | A kind of cake | A rope for climbing
test: Which sentence uses appellation correctly? | I ate my appellation after school | *The shop's appellation, Bella Bakes, was painted over the door | The rain made my appellation wet
exam: Champagne is an appellation on a wine label. What does that tell you? | It is a kind of glass | It means the wine is free | It is the colour of the bottle | *It is a protected name showing the wine comes from one region
